Got your head scarf on, Little Nellie?

@MOL
The college I attended has a small, but fine, art museum, with one VERY minor work by almost every major 20th c. artist. A painting of a chrysanthemum, by Piet Mondrian, before he learned how to draw a square, for instance.

When I was there, it also had a program in which students could borrow artworks--usually prints--for a semester. Was it free, or did they charge $5? I can't remember. But one semester, I had a Picasso hanging on my dorm room wall.

@MOL
I drove through the town, and past the museum, yesterday, but didn't stop; it would have been nice to see the chrysanthemum, though. 
I wish we could edit comments.

@Aaron "given game-related clues are less common"

Less common than . . . ?
Practically everything I know about video games I have learned from the NYT XW. We even had a whole Super Mario themed Sunday fairly recently.

@Desenada 

I emailed to the address above and got an autonomous reply saying they couldn’t change it and maybe  I was using a different device or did it after midnight. I replied to that and it said it would pass it on to the team.

Maybe if enough people complain, they’ll fix it.
